5. DATA PRIVACY AND TELEMETRY

   The Software operates primarily offline. All core data entered into the
   Software — including school information, teachers, classes, subjects, rooms,
   and timetables — is stored locally on the user's device.

   The following telemetry features are ENABLED BY DEFAULT. By installing
   and using the Software, the user consents to the collection of the
   following data by Sepio Corp:

   (a) Registration Data: school name, phone number, email address, address,
       and IP address — used to identify which schools use the application
       and provide better support.
   (b) Anonymous Analytics: non-identifiable event data (e.g., "timetable
       generated", "PDF exported"), session ID, app version, and OS info —
       used to understand which features are most used.
   (c) Crash Reports: error type, message, stack trace, system information,
       and IP address — used to diagnose and fix bugs faster.

   Users can disable any or all telemetry features at any time in
   Settings -> Privacy & Telemetry. Data collected via telemetry is used
   solely for product improvement, bug fixing, and user support, and is
   never sold or shared with third parties.

